The test timed out at 180 s in 4 of 6 full-bundle runs:
- `--quick`: both orders. Result `VERIFY: FAIL (1 failed: tests)`.
- ZTronAssetSyncTests run 1 and run 2: both orders, `✘ Test run with 474 tests in 53 suites failed ... with 4 issues`, 2 time-outs each. Run 3 passed.
- iOS Simulator 6BE15CAF: `failedTests 1`, 'Test exceeded execution time allowance of 3 minutes'.
It also timed out in 1 of 2 runs of the 55-test barrier suite (placeStampsIgnored run 1, load about 9 to 50), and in 1 of 30 isolated runs made six at a time (load about 40).

The instrumented copy (reps-5-2.log) shows the mechanism:
- step 1: `cond=false`, so the first conditions reading had not arrived when R joined;
- R failed with its 500 and entered `failed(.at)` with `transientFailure` set;
- the first satisfied reading counted as an edge and re-queued R, with `now` unchanged and no sleepers;
- step 2: R is `downloading` on its `.hold` step and holds the only slot;
- H stays `queued`, so the wait at :133 never ends.
The engine behaviour is the S3F-1 design. The test lacks the `driving { awaitCondition { $0.state.conditions != nil ... } }` wait that its sibling tests have.

